@@ -3,5 +3,9 @@
 The suite mutates an optional environment entry, the process working directory, and a process-wide
 clock before checking configuration.
 
-Run `npm test`. The second test preserves the state observed before the first test and fails until
-the first test restores every global through immediate and fallback cleanup.
+Run `npm test`. Each mutating case captures the exact starting state, registers local teardown before
+changing globals, and restores that snapshot in `finally`. A per-test fallback covers failures before
+local teardown is registered. Absence and empty-string environment values are preserved separately.
+
+Test files run in parallel in separate processes, so the process-global mutations are isolated while
+the project no longer forces the whole runner to one worker.
